The copy constructor was already a minimal member-init list (base copy plus five scalar copies), so there is nothing to remove; I kept it identical, letting GCC emit the base's vector copy followed by a single packed store for the scalar tail, avoiding any extra work or temporaries.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```